WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
But he [Prater’s father] used to ride his horse to Westlake.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.920
That was the only way they had to get around, mostly horse . . .wagons.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.520
Had a few of them had cars out there, but it wasn't very many.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.500
Do you remember who had cars?

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.600
I'm just curious.

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.500
I'm sure that was a big deal.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:23.620
Had . . . The Rigmaidens had a car, and Garretts had a car, and who else?

8
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.500
Johnson had a car.

9
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.520
That was about it.

10
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.060
Yeah, maybe one or two Braxtons might have had a car.

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.180
It wasn't many cars out there other than wagons.

12
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.080
Because my dad had a horse then after that he got him a wagon.

13
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.100
I didn't hardly ride in the wagon.

14
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:51.360
He didn't get the wagon until after I'd been . . . started working around like that, so I didn't go.

15
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:59.160
He’d . . . After he got the wagon, ride the horse and I used to ride the horse around and about like that.

16
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.060
If I had to go to Westlake or somewhere like that, I’d ride the horse.

17
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:10.420
They'd gather up a bunch of men together from Sulphur, Westlake, Mossville.

18
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:14.780
They all . . . the ones had horses, they'd gather up and had a lot of loose horses,

19
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.500
wild horses up . . . way on up in the woods up there.

20
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.660
They'd ride . . . They’d running horses and catch them.

21
00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:27.840
Horses just turn loose and horses have colts and keep . . . I guess loose horses.

22
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.520
They had a lot of horses all from Mossville on up.

23
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.400
Going up north like that up that woods.

24
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.260
See where Sasol is coming up through?

25
00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.240
All in there is where there used to be horses.

26
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.900
That used to be nothing but woods.

27
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.080
Just woods, you know, no houses or nothing.

28
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.020
The horses lived in the woods?

29
00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.320
Oh yeah.

30
00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:47.960
Wild horses.

31
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.820
They was wild.

32
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:53.380
They'd ride, they'd run them all day long to catch them.

33
00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.200
Ride them.

34
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:54.780
How would they catch them?

35
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.060
They'd rope them. [laughs] Rope.

36
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:56.740
And then what?

37
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.460
Ride them.

38
00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.060
And then the horses . . .

39
00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.460
Or let them loose.

40
00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.660
They took some of them.

41
00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.920
Both white and black used to ride together like that.
